## Layout

```
src/{{ package_name }}/{{ module_id }}/
├── fastapi/           HTTP adapter — router, schemas, dependencies
├── domain/            entities, value objects, domain services (no I/O)
├── application/       use cases + ports (Protocol) in/out
├── infrastructure/    SQLAlchemy repositories, messaging, security
└── tests/             unit · integration (testcontainers) · bdd (pytest-bdd)
```

The dependency direction is one-way: `fastapi → application → domain`, with
`infrastructure` implementing the outbound Protocols. Nothing under `domain/`
imports SQLAlchemy, FastAPI or the broker client — that rule is enforced by
`lint-imports` (see `docs/architecture/backend/standards/python-hexagonal-patterns.md`).

## Run

```bash
uv sync                                  # install from pyproject.toml
cp .env.example .env                     # then fill in the secrets
uv run alembic upgrade head              # apply migrations
uv run uvicorn {{ package_name }}.{{ module_id }}.fastapi.main:app --reload
```

OpenAPI is served at `/docs`; the health probe at `/health`.

## Test

```bash
uv run pytest                            # whole suite
uv run pytest -m "not integration"       # unit only, no containers
uv run pytest --cov={{ package_name }}   # with coverage
```

Integration tests start a real PostgreSQL through testcontainers — Docker must be
running. BDD scenarios live in `tests/bdd/` and are generated from the `.feature`
files by `py-bdd-generator.py`.

## Migrate

```bash
uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "<change>"   # draft from the ORM models
uv run alembic upgrade head                            # apply
uv run alembic downgrade -1                            # roll back one revision
```

Autogenerate only sees models imported by `alembic/env.py` — a new table that is
not imported there produces an empty revision.
